# cw153, the quiet count (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 3: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw153
revision 3
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_jory_barleyton
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the quiet count
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk counts_bars_in_threes_under_the_breath
likes smoked_eel digging sharp_knife autumn_wind
dislikes rats wet_floors
fears a_missed_bar_in_a_batch someone_slipping_near_the_vat
hopes a_safe_count_at_every_shift a_garden_bed_behind_the_house
topics work +0.5 home +0.3 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 weather +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# counts #bars# softly through every shift, keeps a sharp #knife# sheathed, and digs a quiet #garden# when work ends.

words
oath! = Count and clean floor | By the last good bar
saying! = Count once for work and once for safety | A quiet sum can save a day
count = count | careful count
number = number | small number
numbers = numbers | small numbers
sum = sum | final sum
mark = mark | counting mark
marks = marks | counting marks
bar = bar | soap bar
bars = bars | soap bars
soap = soap | firm soap
batch = batch | boiling batch
vat = vat | hot vat
vats = vats | boiling vats
lye = lye | strong lye
ash = ash | sifted ash
fat = fat | rendered fat
water = water | clear water
fire = fire | low fire
heat = heat | steady heat
paddle = paddle | stirring paddle
ladle = ladle | long ladle
mould = mould | soap mould
moulds = moulds | soap moulds
shelf = shelf | drying shelf
shelves = shelves | drying shelves
floor = floor | workroom floor
plank = plank | floor plank
bucket = bucket | water bucket
cloth = cloth | dry cloth
knife = knife | sharp knife
blade = blade | clean blade
edge = edge | keen edge
sheath = sheath | knife sheath
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
worker = worker | fellow worker
workers = workers | work crew
garden = garden | small garden
bed = bed | garden bed
beds = beds | garden beds
soil = soil | garden soil
spade = spade | digging spade
root = root | sound root
roots = roots | sound roots
weed = weed | garden weed
weeds = weeds | garden weeds
wind = wind | autumn wind
autumn = autumn | leaf season
rain = rain | shower
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lakeshore
eel = eel | smoked eel
smoke = smoke | cooking smoke
plate = plate | supper plate
bread = bread | loaf
loaf = loaf | bread loaf
tea = tea | cup of tea
cup = cup | warm cup
rat = rat | larder rat
rats = rats | larder rats
larder = larder | food cupboard
home = home | shared cottage
house = house | shared house
spouse = spouse | partner
family = family | household
table = table | supper table
pot = pot | supper pot
door = door | front door
roof = roof | sound roof
market = market | market square
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | earned coin
city = city | Ridgemere
street = street | city street
road = road | High Road
bench = bench | wooden bench
hour = hour | passing hour
hours = hours | passing hours
night = night | late night
morning = morning | early morning

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : A #city# can make a working #hand# disappear in its crowd. | The #shore# lets me recognize the turns toward #home#.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Give a hungry #worker# #bread# today. | A small #sum# from many #hands# can fill a #table#.
opinion @1 drink mixed 0 : I like a #cup# after the #vat# cools. | Nobody should handle hot #lye# after too much drink.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : The #market# can be pleasant when work is done. | I still prefer a quieter #table# afterward.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A fine house has room to leave a #bench# empty. | The #workers# I know wait outside its #door#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #bread# #price# goes up while our pay stays still. | Supper comes after I have counted the remaining #coin#.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : Let a new #hand# practise the #count# slowly. | I will show where the dry #floor# begins.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A #stranger# can have a #plate# while we talk. | The #house# has made room for a new face before.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Each #batch# is hard work, yet the #coin# stretches less. | I hope the next week is easier on our #table#.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. I am at the middle of a #count#. | #greet#. The #floor# is damp; step near the #door#.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Let me finish these last three #bars#. | Speak as I carry this #bucket# across.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Your #plate# of #eel# is near the #fire#. | I kept the #bench# beside the #fire# clear.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #vat# is not hot yet. | #greet#. I have counted the #moulds# before breakfast.
line @1 greet.return : I remember where the #count# stopped. | #welcome_back#. This #batch# is nearly finished.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come inside; I cleared your place at the #table#. | There is #bread# left for you.
line @1 again.open : I had one #number# left to check when you went. | Did we finish talking about the #garden#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Mind the wet #plank#. | #saying.capitalize#. This #knife# belongs in its #sheath#.
line @1 farewell.return : Perhaps the new #garden# #bed# will be turned when you return. | We can share another #plate# then.
line @1 react.news : Wait until I have finished this #sum#. | Which part did you see yourself?
line @1 react.news.new : Nobody in the workroom mentioned it. | Who brought the account to the #shore#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a smaller version at supper. | Your details add up differently.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would check each #number# before repeating it. | One missing piece changes the whole #sum#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is a loss no one should carry alone; I will stay nearby. | There is a #bench# here while the #bars# rest.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That brings a good #sum# to the day. | Let their household share an extra #plate# tonight.
line @1 answer.how : #work.capitalize# has gone steadily. | I have supper to look forward to.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am counting the next #batch#. | The #floor# needs drying before we carry anything else.
line @1 ask.how : Did your #hands# get a rest? | Has your #home# been quiet?
line @1 sympathise : I can listen while you sit. | A warm #cup# may help before we speak.
line @1 reassure : We can recount the #bars# and find what is missing. | The #garden# will still be there tomorrow.
line @1 decline : I cannot leave this #vat# unattended. | No, that #floor# is too slick to cross with a #bucket#.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand. I will carry the #bucket# myself. | Very well; we can try another time.
line @1 thank : You set a dry #cloth# on the #floor# before I slipped. | The #bars# were counted when I returned; thank you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I only moved the #bucket# aside. | There was an extra #plate# at #home#.
line @1 preclose : The #moulds# must be set out before dark. | I have a #garden# #bed# to turn.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You lost count before reaching five #bars#. | Your #spade# has done more resting than digging.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will check the #marks#. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #knife# stays sheathed.
line @1 give.advice : Dry the #floor# before lifting a full #ladle#. | Count the #moulds# after filling them.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep company on the #road# tonight. | We should bring the #bucket# work indoors early.
scene three_at_time
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #bars# in threes while moving them to the #shelf#. | It leaves a small group to check if someone calls me away.
b : Does that help? | Do you ever lose your place?
a : Most days. | Then I start the group again.

scene quiet_numbers
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count under my breath while walking #home#. | It slows my thoughts after the noise of the #vat#.
b : What do you count? | Does anyone notice?
a : The steps to the #door#. | Only someone walking close.

scene dry_floor
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A wet #floor# near the #vat# worries me more than a slow #batch#. | I stop and spread a #cloth# before the next #ladle# moves.
b : Does the crew wait? | Has anyone slipped?
a : Long enough to stay safe. | Once was enough to teach us.

scene sharp_edge
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep a #knife# #edge# clean for cutting #soap# from a #mould#. | A dull cut makes the #bar# crumble.
b : When does the #edge# need work? | Is it safe to carry?
a : Before a large #batch#. | In its #sheath#.

scene garden_spade
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An #hour# digging in the #garden# feels different from stirring a #vat#. | I decide when to rest the #spade# against the wall.
b : Does anything grow there? | Do you work alone?
a : A few good #roots#. | Often, until supper.

scene first_roots
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I left one #bed# of #soil# loose enough for the first #roots#. | The #weeds# returned before the plants did.
b : Did you pull them? | Was the planting lost?
a : Every morning. | The small plants came through.

scene smoked_eel
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I bring smoked #eel# #home# when the #market# has it. | A little goes a long way with #bread#.
b : Do you warm it by the #fire#? | Is it your favourite supper?
a : Just warm it. | After a long #batch#, yes.

scene larder_rat
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #bread# before shutting the #larder#. | A #rat# found the bottom #shelf# once and left crumbs.
b : Did you catch it? | Was much taken?
a : After moving the food higher. | One corner of a #loaf#.

scene autumn_wind
when topic=weather here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Autumn #wind# clears the #smoke# from the workroom #door#. | I stand outside for a breath before going back to the #vat#.
b : Does it cool the room? | Do the others join you?
a : Only near the #door#. | When the #batch# allows.

scene cold_tea
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I dislike #tea# that has cooled while I count #moulds#. | I make a fresh #cup# rather than pretend the first is pleasant.
b : Does that waste it? | Can you keep it near the #fire#?
a : A little. | Away from the #lye#, yes.

scene mould_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I mark each #mould# as it is filled. | The #sum# at the end should match the #bars# on the drying #shelf#.
b : What if it does not? | Do you recount them?
a : I look for a cracked one. | By groups of three.

scene water_bucket
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I carry less #water# than the #bucket# can hold. | A full one sloshes over the #floor# beside the hot #vat#.
b : Does that mean more trips? | Is it worth it?
a : One extra. | We keep our footing.

scene spouse_supper
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #self.spouse# hears my counting continue after the workroom is closed. | Supper draws me back to the #table#.
b : Do you talk about the work? | Does the counting stop?
a : After the first #plate#. | Once I have eaten.

scene shared_house
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #house# has workers returning at different #hours#. | I leave a #plate# near the #fire# for whoever comes late.
b : Is there room for everyone? | Do you stay awake?
a : Around the #table#, yes. | Until the last #door# closes.

scene fair_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count what a #loaf# costs before I leave the #market#. | It is easier than finding too little #coin# at the stall.
b : Does the price change often? | Do you buy anything else?
a : More than I like. | #eel# if there is room.

scene city_crowd
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #city# crowd would make me lose my count before the second #street#. | I prefer the #shore# where my steps have room.
b : Have you been there? | Would you go again?
a : For a short errand. | Only if #work# requires it.

scene new_worker
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I show a new #worker# the dry way around the #vat#. | Then I ask for a count of the cold #bars#.
b : Do they learn quickly? | Why cold bars first?
a : When they take their time. | Safe mistakes are easier to mend.

story missing_bar [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : I counted a #batch# and found one #bar# missing from the #shelf#.
  : It had slipped behind a #mould#, still sound but out of sight.
  b : Your count caught it. Did you find it quickly?
  : After checking each group of three.

story wet_plank [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : A #bucket# spilled across a #plank# just as a worker lifted a #ladle#.
  : I called a stop, dried the #floor#, and only then let the #ladle# pass.
  ask : Did anyone fall?
  b : Good that you saw it.
  : No. We lost a little time and nothing else.

story garden_root [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I dug a #garden# #bed# after a long day beside the #vat#.
  : One #root# from last season was still sound beneath the #soil#.
  b : A small reward for digging. Did you keep it?
  : It went into the supper #pot#.

rule @bark_count
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One, two, three. Start the next #shelf#. | That #sum# needs checking.

rule @bark_floor
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Dry the #floor# before moving the #ladle#. | The #bucket# can wait here.

rule @bark_garden
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #garden# #bed# has new #weeds#. | I will turn the #soil# after work.

rule @bark_tea
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say My #tea# has gone cold again. | A fresh #cup# after this #batch#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I am counting the #bars# before they dry. | #greet#. Mind the damp #floor# beside the #vat#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back for another #batch#? | Your visit has come just before I finish this #count#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I help make #soap# at #self.workplace# and count each #batch#. | At #self.workplace#, I carry cooled #bars# from #vat# to drying #shelves#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep clear of the wet #plank#. | #saying.capitalize#. I have the #moulds# to count.
graft resident.hub
choice Why count the bars twice? -> count
node count
say A #bar# can slip behind a #mould# or a #shelf#. I count as we make them and again when they dry.
free
choice What do you do after work? -> garden
choice Back to the workroom. -> hub
node garden
say I dig in the #garden# when the #vat# is done. It lets me stop counting for a while.
choice Back to the workroom. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
